      "side": 1,
      "message": "The commit message frames this as a pure type conversion, but the change also moves the read of num_hyp_event_mods in __pkvm_sync_ftrace from outside the lock to inside it. Before, the count was snapshot before hyp_spin_lock(), so a concurrent register_hyp_mod_events() could add a module between the read and the lock acquire, and __pkvm_sync_ftrace would miss it. After, the read is under the lock and sees the latest value.\n\nThat is a behavioral fix worth calling out in the commit message, not just a side effect of dropping atomic_t.",
      "revId": "89c75fea172ec3e1df51707b3a16456e83590eef",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
